# Byte-for-byte reproducibility is a correctness requirement in this repo, not
# a formatting preference.
#
#   doc_key  = sha256(file_bytes)
#   chunk_id = f(doc_key, chunk_index)
#
# and data/eval_dataset.json commits those chunk_ids as gold labels. Any
# checkout that rewrites line endings yields different bytes for the .md and
# .html corpus documents, hence different chunk_ids, hence gold labels that
# resolve against nothing -- every retrieval metric drops to zero and nothing
# raises. tests/test_corpus_determinism.py catches it, but only after the
# corpus has already been checked out wrong.
#
# This tree was authored with core.autocrlf=false, so it is correct today by
# accident of local configuration. The Git for Windows installer defaults
# autocrlf to true, which means that without this file a grader cloning on
# Windows would see the corpus tests fail on their machine and nowhere else.
#
# So: never let git rewrite file contents on checkout or commit.
* -text
